Correct the position of a tilted DFT pen (TiltOffsetLinear, TiltOffsetQuadratic)

The position that is measured is where the field of the tip electrode is strongest on the
sensor. With a tilted pen that is not the point of the tip but a place shifted towards the body
of the pen. The shift grows with the distance d between the tip and the ring centroid (in
antennas): the correction is TiltOffsetQuadratic * d^2 + TiltOffsetLinear * d antennas in the
direction from the ring to the tip, smoothed with TiltOffsetGain per sample (0.1) and dropped
when it exceeds half an antenna. Off by default (both 0); needs ExtraPositionWindows.

With 0.0089 and 0.0402 on the Surface Pro 9 with the Slim Pen 2 the correction is 0.05 mm in
upright handwriting and 0.19 .. 0.29 mm with the pen at 26 .. 37 degrees. Measured against the
Windows reference position for the same frames: median distance of the
contact samples 0.03 .. 0.27 mm before, 0.04 .. 0.10 mm after; the remaining difference has a
constant part of about 0.02 mm per axis, which is rounding on the other side.

